      "passageTitle": "Questions 129-132 refer to the following press release.",
      "passageHtml": "<div class=\"passage-box article-format\">\n<p style=\"color:#718096; font-size:0.9rem;\">FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE</p>\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:4px; font-size:1.2rem;\">AURORA BIOTECH EXPANDS EUROPEAN FOOTPRINT WITH NEW MUNICH RESEARCH HUB</h3>\n<p><strong>MUNICH (April 9)</strong> — Aurora Biotech, an emerging leader in sustainable agricultural technology, announced today that it will establish a 25,000-square-meter research and development center in Munich, Germany. The facility is expected to become fully operational by the second quarter of next year.</p>\n<p>The state-of-the-art facility will concentrate primarily on creating drought-resistant crop varieties and eco-friendly organic fertilizers. According to Chief Executive Officer Marcus Vance, the strategic location was selected due to Munich's thriving biotechnology ecosystem and its proximity to top European research universities.</p>\n<p>To support this expansion, Aurora Biotech intends to recruit more than 150 specialists, including geneticists, agronomists, and laboratory technicians, over the next eighteen months. Furthermore, the company recently <u>secured</u> €45 million in private venture funding to finance the center's specialized laboratory apparatus.</p>\n<p>Job openings will be posted on Aurora Biotech’s careers portal beginning in June, with initial interviews scheduled throughout July and August.</p>\n</div>",
